<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regency period (Brazil)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1831–1840</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Regency period</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regency period was the era from 1831 to 1840 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> was governed by regents on behalf of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a> after his father's abdication. It was marked by serial provincial rebellions, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cabanagem">Cabanagem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a>. It ended when Pedro II was declared of age in 1840, stabilising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p></div>
